# Gitignored files that worktrees need, in gitignore syntax.

# The dogfooding links scripts/link-skills.sh writes. They are RELATIVE
# symlinks, so a copied link resolves against the worktree's own skills/ and
# agents/ — each lane dogfoods the branch it is working on, not the main
# checkout. Without these a lane runs against whatever is installed globally,
# which is the opposite of dogfooding.
.claude/skills/
.claude/agents/

# Deliberately absent: dependencies (the Setup command's job — a copied tree
# carries platform-specific builds and drifts from the lockfile) and .scratch
# (plans are reached by absolute path into the main worktree).

# MUST stay last — gitignore matching is last-match-wins, so only the final
# position reliably stops copy mechanisms cloning existing worktrees into a new one.
!.claude/worktrees/**
